Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Add Signal & Noise stage under Review; fix WorkMap crash
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Signal & Noise is a ledger-derived read of live time, added as the second
stage under Review so the StageBar renders automatically (no shell change).

- Signal = live hours that produced a validated outcome a receipt can point
  to; noise = every other hour, decomposed into five named classes, each
  routing (click-through) to the lever that reduces it.
- Numbers derive from LIVE_TIME_GOVERNANCE (186 total / 52 recoverable) and
  ORG_LOAD, so this screen can never disagree with Executive Review. The
  fifth noise class takes the remainder so classes always sum to recoverable.
- Monochrome only: distinctions carried by fill density, no color/gauge, no
  individual scoring. Editorial ratio, declared noise floor with target line,
  quarterly redraw citing real REDRAW_MEASURED interventions, per-org multiples.
- Removes the committed `throw new Error('TEMP boundary test…')` at the top of
  WorkMap, which had killed Evidence → Relationships in production.

Verified: tsc --noEmit clean, vite build green, lever navigation and WorkMap
render confirmed via headless browser.

