 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=202=C3=972=20scatter=20with=20hover?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A quadrant view on the Signal & Noise stage: every call this week is a dot,
positioned by real Meeting fields so placement is ledger-derived —
  Y = readinessScore (outcome / did it produce a receipt)
  X = necessityScore (did it need to be live)
Dot size = attendee-hours at stake. Quadrants map onto the noise decomposition:
Signal (top-right), Async-eligible (top-left), At risk (bottom-right, deferral /
rework), Noise (bottom-left).

Hover (or focus) a dot for a tooltip: the call, its quadrant, a single signal
score, and the outcome / live-need / hours / value breakdown — enough to read,
not enough to overwhelm. Monochrome, hand-rolled CSS, no chart library.

The four real MEETINGS (minus the focus block) seed WEEK_CALLS so the matrix
can't drift from the day's actual scores; the rest are the week's other calls.

Verified: tsc clean, vite build green, tooltip + focus paths confirmed headless.

