Per direction, Signal & Noise is no longer a stage under Review — it is its own
admin-only module for testing the app's data against the app.

Packaging (same repo, separate build):
- __ADMIN_TOOLS__ build flag via Vite define (VITE_ADMIN_TOOLS). The public
  `npm run build` compiles the module — screens and their imports — OUT of the
  bundle entirely (verified: 0 admin strings in dist/, 24 KB lighter, rail shows
  only the six public destinations). `npm run build:admin` → dist-admin/ includes
  it, for a separate access-restricted deploy.

Module (rail destination "Signal & Noise · Admin · data integrity", 3 stages):
- View        — the derived signal/noise instrument (moved out of Review).
- Reconciliation — live pass/fail tie-out checks (12) against the app's own
  constants and internal invariants; green = trustworthy, red = drift.
- Raw data    — source figures next to the derived model and every scored call.

Data seam: src/data/adapters.ts is the single boundary the module uses to reach
the app's data — swap it to a real API later with no downstream changes. Scoring
helpers extracted to src/data/signalNoiseMath.ts so the checks verify with the
exact functions the view renders with, not a re-implementation.

Also: Review reverts to a single stage.

Verified: tsc clean; public + admin builds green; admin screens render; 12/12
checks pass; no runtime errors; public rail excludes the module.

